IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-income`
IMPORT `itaa-super`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- amounts this naive encoding takes as inputs that the
-- Federal Register's formula images now give: net labour income (s 61-155(2)) for `the working Australians tax offset`, and
-- the concessional contributions cap and the general transfer balance cap for any year (ss 291-20(2), 294-35(3), indexed under
-- s 960-285) for `the non-concessional contributions cap` and `the transfer balance cap on first having an account`.
--
-- A module beside itaa-income.l4 and itaa-super.l4 (24 October 2026). They stay as they are; this module calls them. The
-- baseline encoding (../baseline-2026-10/, itaa-income-formulas.l4 and itaa-super-formulas.l4) carries the same formulas with
-- seat questions; this naive module is kept to the three inputs above, in the naive style (no @export).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267 (register id C2026C00400), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt; the
-- formulas from ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md (entries s 61-155(2) and s 960-285(5), recovered
-- 2026-10-24). The AWOTE and CPI index numbers (s 960-285(7), s 960-280(1), (4)) are published figures, not deposited: inputs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Not for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- naive inputs now computed`

-- s 61-155(2):   Labour amounts − Labour deductions
GIVEN `labour amounts` IS A NUMBER, `labour deductions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net labour income` MEANS
    `labour amounts` MINUS `labour deductions`

-- `the working Australians tax offset` with net labour income worked out (the threshold and the notional liability stay inputs).
GIVEN `resident at any time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN, `labour amounts` IS A NUMBER, `labour deductions` IS A NUMBER,
      `tax-free threshold` IS A NUMBER, `basic liability on net labour income alone` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the working Australians tax offset from labour amounts` MEANS
    `the working Australians tax offset` `resident at any time in the year` (`the net labour income` `labour amounts` `labour deductions`)
        `tax-free threshold` `basic liability on net labour income alone`

-- s 960-285(5), (6): factor = index number for the December quarter before the year / index number for the base quarter (31
-- December 2016 for both caps), to 3 decimal places rounding up from 5. (2): base amount x factor, rounded down to the rounding
-- amount ($2,500 for the concessional cap, item 2; $100,000 for the general transfer balance cap, item 3). (4): not indexed if
-- the factor is 1 or less.
GIVEN `base amount` IS A NUMBER, `rounding amount` IS A NUMBER, `index now` IS A NUMBER, `index at base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indexed under 960-285` MEANS
    IF `factor` AT MOST 1 THEN `base amount`
    ELSE FLOOR (`base amount` TIMES `factor` DIVIDED BY `rounding amount`) TIMES `rounding amount`
    WHERE
        `factor` MEANS FLOOR ((`index now` DIVIDED BY `index at base`) TIMES 1000 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000

-- s 291-20(2) ($25,000 for 2017-18; AWOTE) and s 294-35(3) ($1,600,000 for 2017-18; CPI), for 2017-18 or later.
GIVEN `AWOTE for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER, `AWOTE for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concessional contributions cap from AWOTE` MEANS
    `indexed under 960-285` 25000 2500 `AWOTE for the December quarter before the year` `AWOTE for the December 2016 quarter`

GIVEN `CPI for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER, `CPI for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the general transfer balance cap from CPI` MEANS
    `indexed under 960-285` 1600000 100000 `CPI for the December quarter before the year` `CPI for the December 2016 quarter`

GIVEN `AWOTE for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER, `AWOTE for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER,
      `CPI for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER, `CPI for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER,
      `total superannuation balance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-concessional contributions cap from the index numbers` MEANS
    `the non-concessional contributions cap`
        (`the concessional contributions cap from AWOTE` `AWOTE for the December quarter before the year` `AWOTE for the December 2016 quarter`)
        `total superannuation balance`
        (`the general transfer balance cap from CPI` `CPI for the December quarter before the year` `CPI for the December 2016 quarter`)

GIVEN `first financial year starting` IS A NUMBER, `CPI for the December quarter before the year` IS A NUMBER,
      `CPI for the December 2016 quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transfer balance cap on first having an account from CPI` MEANS
    `the transfer balance cap on first having an account` `first financial year starting`
        (`the general transfer balance cap from CPI` `CPI for the December quarter before the year` `CPI for the December 2016 quarter`)
